<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $1.075 bln in March 12 wk.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $1.075 bln in March 12 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $1.075 billion to $44.670 billion in the week ended March 12, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $1.058 billion to $44.940 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $2.69  billion to $819.805 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
